import LeanOS.Wifi.NPhy

/-
Radio 2056 power-up and 2.4 GHz channel programming for the BCM43224
(N-PHY rev 6, radio 2056 rev 11, 20 MHz, internal PA in 2.4 GHz).

Ported from Linux brcmsmac (ISC license), Copyright (c) 2010 Broadcom
Corporation; see drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac at Linux
commit fd179f8a05be3ccae366b9b96e176b51fbe54aab.

Entry points:
* `radioOn cfg` — `wlc_phy_switch_radio(pi, ON)` for N-PHY rev 3..6:
  preinit, default register tables, postinit, then `wlc_phy_chanspec_set`.
* `chanspecSet cfg` — `wlc_phy_chanspec_set` alone (retune).

Context assumed (brcmsmac `wlc_phy_init`, phy_cmn.c:707-750): the MAC is
disabled (`wlc_phy_init` WARNs if `MCTL_EN_MAC` is set) and this is the first
PHY init after attach (`phy_init_por` true, `radio_is_on` false, all
"adjusted" spur-war flags false). Nothing on this path suspends or enables
the MAC for D11 core rev 23 (the classifier's MAC suspend is rev 16 only), so
no suspend/enable code is emitted; a later retune must likewise be issued
with the MAC suspended by the caller.

Attach-time values used (all decided while generating):
* `pi->bw = WL_CHANSPEC_BW_20` (phy_cmn.c:481) so `wlapi_bmac_bw_set` is not
  called; the band is 2.4 GHz so every `CHSPEC_IS5G` branch is pruned.
* `ipa2g_on = (fem2g.extpagain == 2)` → `cfg.ipa2g` (true on the Qotom).
* `phy_corenum = 2`; `phy_spuravoid = SPURAVOID_AUTO` (phy_cmn.c:308-312);
  `nphy_txpwrctrl = PHY_TPC_HW_ON` for rev >= 3 (phy_n.c:14355-14359) so
  `wlc_phy_txpwr_fixpower_nphy` is not called; `phyhang_avoid = false` for
  rev 6 (phy_n.c:14604-14605); `nphy_gband_spurwar_en = true`,
  `nphy_aband_spurwar_en` / `nphy_gband_spurwar2_en` from boardflags2
  (phy_n.c:14607-14615).
-/
namespace LeanOS.Wifi.Radio2056

open LeanOS.Wifi.Bytecode LeanOS.Wifi.Bcm43224 LeanOS.Wifi.NPhy

